1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Upkeep you only notice when something beeps.

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:16,740
A real MCP server, spec 2025-11-25 over Streamable HTTP, behind a simulated Alexa+ experience.

3
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,860
The simulator speaks first.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,120
Dryer vent cleaning is twenty-one days overdue, and the fridge water filter is due today.

5
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:32,300
Exact-fit part, policy filter, code-gated mock purchase.

6
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:40,540
The certified CX-28 is the cheapest filter the rules allow, and an uncertified one is filtered out.

7
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:49,920
After a masked purchase code, a mock order is placed, with no real payment.

8
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:58,780
Get upkeep status, resolve appliance, and find parts all returned two hundred.

9
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:02,140
It uses what you already own.

10
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:09,180
Two nine-volt batteries are already on the garage shelf, so nothing is bought, and a swap task is added.

11
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:15,740
After the swap, one nine-volt is left, and the next change is due October 2027.

12
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:20,100
It places a mock booking with the pro. The limit is enforced by the server.

13
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:25,520
The earliest opening is Tuesday, nine to eleven, for eighty-nine dollars.

14
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:31,120
That is over the sixty dollar limit, so it needs approval and the purchase code.

15
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:37,280
The mock booking for Tuesday morning is confirmed, with no real purchase or payment.

16
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:44,720
New session, same memory. Safety beats shopping.

17
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:50,560
The next morning, the filter has shipped, and the vent cleaning is still booked for Tuesday.

18
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:55,320
For a gas smell, it tells you to leave the home and call your local emergency number.

19
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:00,960
Verifiable protocol behaviour, and open source.

20
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:04,240
The trace shows the raw JSON for this session.

21
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:13,240
It is MIT licensed, with npm test and npm run test e2e.

22
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:19,840
Fictional sample data. Simulated Alexa+ experience.

